WEBVTT

00:00:27.190 --> 00:00:29.490
That was indeed a close call.

00:00:29.490 --> 00:00:31.190
Not very subtle.

00:00:31.190 --> 00:00:35.030
There won't be any witnesses up
here in the mountains, after all.

00:00:35.030 --> 00:00:38.400
They probably plan to chalk up
the fire to suspected arson.

00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:40.040
How did they know about this place?

00:00:40.040 --> 00:00:45.600
I was able to find you. It's not
like ISDA wouldn't be able to.

00:00:47.540 --> 00:00:50.450
They're bound to figure out
that they came up empty.

00:00:50.450 --> 00:00:52.110
They'll be after us soon.

00:00:52.110 --> 00:00:54.380
Where are we going?

00:00:54.380 --> 00:00:56.180
To Tokyo.

00:01:15.100 --> 00:01:20.810
In my younger days, I lost

00:01:20.810 --> 00:01:26.720
even the reason for this pain

00:01:26.720 --> 00:01:32.420
Crouching over, making excuses

00:01:32.420 --> 00:01:35.620
I must have...

00:01:37.060 --> 00:01:43.330
Taking hold of the premonition
I saw at the end of the blue,

00:01:43.330 --> 00:01:50.910
riding the wind, I'm off
to where the light shines

00:01:50.910 --> 00:01:53.780
I'll always be with you

00:01:53.780 --> 00:01:56.280
see the sky in front of you

00:01:56.280 --> 00:02:00.650
fly high in a light from the deepest blue

00:02:02.450 --> 00:02:07.990
Riding the echo of swirling stars,

00:02:07.990 --> 00:02:10.660
I sing out

00:02:10.660 --> 00:02:19.330
May my voice reach you

00:02:37.290 --> 00:02:40.690
Won't it create a problem for us,
being so publicly exposed?

00:02:40.690 --> 00:02:43.120
To hide a tree, you put it in the forest;

00:02:43.120 --> 00:02:45.330
to hide a person, you put
them with other people.

00:02:45.330 --> 00:02:47.360
We'd draw more suspicion if we sneak around.

00:02:47.360 --> 00:02:50.130
Nobody has seen you, so you're fine.

00:02:50.130 --> 00:02:52.470
A little too self-conscious, aren't we?

00:02:52.470 --> 00:02:54.200
Well, excuse me.

00:02:59.370 --> 00:03:02.140
There's another reason for coming to Tokyo.

00:03:02.140 --> 00:03:06.850
Right now, Tartarus is one
of the most heavily secured

00:03:06.850 --> 00:03:09.920
facilities that ISDA controls.

00:03:09.920 --> 00:03:13.820
We'll need all sorts of preparation
and equipment to break in.

00:03:13.820 --> 00:03:18.090
ISDA isn't about to let us take
their regular ferry there, right?

00:03:18.090 --> 00:03:19.830
Little man...

00:03:19.830 --> 00:03:23.400
What I mean is, we'll come by more information

00:03:23.400 --> 00:03:26.270
and illegal goods where
there are more people around.

00:03:26.270 --> 00:03:29.670
It doesn't do anyone any good
if we're not ready before we act,

00:03:29.670 --> 00:03:31.710
and we wind up getting caught.

00:03:31.710 --> 00:03:35.680
But are there any safe hideouts in Tokyo?

00:03:35.680 --> 00:03:38.280
It's going to be hard to keep
ourselves completely hidden

00:03:38.280 --> 00:03:41.050
from ISDA, even in Tokyo.

00:03:41.050 --> 00:03:44.190
- So then...
- Hey, even if they find out where we are,

00:03:44.190 --> 00:03:47.120
as long as we're someplace they
won't strike at us, we're fine.

00:03:47.120 --> 00:03:49.290
And is there such a convenient location?

00:03:49.290 --> 00:03:51.030
There is.

00:03:51.030 --> 00:03:53.690
Don't tell me the place you mean is...

00:04:02.240 --> 00:04:05.770
- Here?
- Sigelinde's family home.

00:04:05.770 --> 00:04:09.410
"Little" man, that goes for your brain, too.

00:04:09.410 --> 00:04:10.550
Wha...?

00:04:10.550 --> 00:04:13.820
Do you seriously think that
my family home is in Japan?

00:04:13.820 --> 00:04:17.590
The Baumgards are one of the
foremost noble families in Germany.

00:04:17.590 --> 00:04:20.590
Your mansion is in Nuremberg,
as I recall, isn't it?

00:04:20.590 --> 00:04:25.090
That's right. This is the vacation house
we use when we stay in Japan.

00:04:25.090 --> 00:04:28.090
- Vacation house?!
- Got a problem with that?

00:04:29.400 --> 00:04:33.060
This isn't a house, it's a castle.

00:04:37.440 --> 00:04:40.310
Welcome home, Young Miss.

00:04:46.250 --> 00:04:48.750
I-It's huge.

00:04:48.750 --> 00:04:50.320
Say...

00:04:50.320 --> 00:04:51.910
Up there.

00:04:57.190 --> 00:04:59.990
A-Amadeus!

00:04:59.990 --> 00:05:03.770
That portrait is of Alfred-sama.

00:05:03.770 --> 00:05:07.500
The gentleman who is
Lady Sigelinde's grandfather.

00:05:07.500 --> 00:05:10.700
Sigelinde's grandfather?

00:05:12.510 --> 00:05:16.340
It has been too long, Sigelinde.

00:05:16.340 --> 00:05:19.050
There's no reason to be so surprised.

00:05:19.050 --> 00:05:22.520
You're not the only one who uses this mansion.

00:05:22.520 --> 00:05:26.690
He just arrived today, saying
he had a meeting in Japan.

00:05:26.690 --> 00:05:29.620
Wilhelm Baumgard,

00:05:29.620 --> 00:05:31.830
the current head of the Baumgard family.

00:05:31.830 --> 00:05:34.690
Then, he's Sigelinde's father?

00:05:37.900 --> 00:05:42.540
- Had dinner?
- Not yet, but I don't feel like eating.

00:05:42.540 --> 00:05:44.740
I wasn't asking you.

00:05:44.740 --> 00:05:49.140
You should be more mindful about
entertaining when we have guests.

00:05:49.140 --> 00:05:53.210
Father, unfortunately, I will
be excusing myself now.

00:05:53.210 --> 00:05:54.850
H-Hey...

00:05:54.850 --> 00:05:58.380
If you leave now, you'll
have nowhere else to go.

00:06:01.420 --> 00:06:04.690
You'll be safe here.

00:06:04.690 --> 00:06:07.230
Are you saying you'd be kind enough to hide us?

00:06:07.230 --> 00:06:09.860
Of course I will.

00:06:09.860 --> 00:06:13.000
You are the heiress to the Baumgard family.

00:06:13.000 --> 00:06:15.670
I have no intention of
handing you over to the ones

00:06:15.670 --> 00:06:17.930
who are chasing those reptiles around.

00:06:24.780 --> 00:06:29.580
The Baumgard family has been
backing ISDA, to some extent.

00:06:29.580 --> 00:06:31.450
As long as you are in this mansion,

00:06:31.450 --> 00:06:34.960
they will not be so indiscreet
as to come after you.

00:06:34.960 --> 00:06:38.450
But that is all that I can do.

00:06:40.360 --> 00:06:43.930
It will be plenty. If you can
buy us a few days' time,

00:06:43.930 --> 00:06:46.600
we'll manage the rest on our own.

00:06:46.600 --> 00:06:48.260
I see.

00:06:52.940 --> 00:06:55.410
I am terribly sorry for interrupting your meal,

00:06:55.410 --> 00:06:58.980
but there is an urgent call
from the home country for you.

00:06:58.980 --> 00:07:00.420
Okay.

00:07:00.420 --> 00:07:04.580
I'm sorry, but if you would please excuse me...

00:07:09.790 --> 00:07:13.830
You didn't know he was here
when you brought us here, right?

00:07:13.830 --> 00:07:15.460
Nonsense.

00:07:15.460 --> 00:07:18.800
I have to admit, if you're financing ISDA,

00:07:18.800 --> 00:07:22.240
then your family really is wealthy, huh?

00:07:22.240 --> 00:07:24.140
They're not my family.

00:07:29.780 --> 00:07:31.510
Sigelinde...

00:07:32.980 --> 00:07:35.420
An anti-Thanatos factor?

00:07:35.420 --> 00:07:39.750
Yes. Once we inject this
anti-Thanatos factor into the cells

00:07:39.750 --> 00:07:43.660
we extracted from the Raum...
Please see for yourselves.

00:07:43.660 --> 00:07:46.860
Once within the Dragon cells,
the anti-Thanatos factor

00:07:46.860 --> 00:07:50.270
causes repetitive irregular division,
as with cancer cells,

00:07:50.270 --> 00:07:53.470
and eats away at the normal cells.

00:07:53.470 --> 00:07:56.870
Soon, the normal cells die out.

00:07:56.870 --> 00:08:01.980
Thanatos is still an organism,
and cannot maintain its life like this.

00:08:01.980 --> 00:08:05.280
But how do we get that factor inside Thanatos?

00:08:05.280 --> 00:08:07.850
- We use the Dragons.
- Dragons?!

00:08:07.850 --> 00:08:11.350
Yes. In order for the factor to
take effect, it will be necessary

00:08:11.350 --> 00:08:15.020
to introduce it into Thanatos
in an activated state.

00:08:15.020 --> 00:08:19.030
So, first we introduce the factor
into a Dragon, and afterward,

00:08:19.030 --> 00:08:22.000
send the whole Dragon,
as a host, inside Thanatos.

00:08:22.000 --> 00:08:24.300
Like sending rats that are infected
with disease-causing germs

00:08:24.300 --> 00:08:29.370
into the enemy camp. It would be
a primitive biological weapon.

00:08:29.370 --> 00:08:30.910
I get it.

00:08:30.910 --> 00:08:35.380
But I thought we were using the
Dragon Slayer against Thanatos.

00:08:35.380 --> 00:08:37.850
We will still move forward with the operation

00:08:37.850 --> 00:08:40.550
that makes use of the Dragon Slayer, of course.

00:08:40.550 --> 00:08:44.550
But the goal of D Project
is to destroy Thanatos,

00:08:44.550 --> 00:08:47.760
regardless of the methods used.

00:08:47.760 --> 00:08:52.890
Indeed, there's no harm in having
many ways of defeating the enemy.

00:08:52.890 --> 00:08:57.230
We have already begun experiments
using Howling Star and Amadeus.

00:08:57.230 --> 00:08:58.930
When will you know the results?

00:08:58.930 --> 00:09:03.100
We've scheduled our first examination tomorrow.

00:09:03.100 --> 00:09:04.940
Tomorrow, huh?

00:09:09.110 --> 00:09:13.920
Say, Sigelinde, are you awake?

00:09:13.920 --> 00:09:15.250
What?

00:09:15.250 --> 00:09:19.250
What does it feel like to have a father?

00:09:19.250 --> 00:09:20.960
Where did that come from?

00:09:20.960 --> 00:09:27.760
I was created from Thanatos.
I don't have a father or a mother, so...

00:09:27.760 --> 00:09:29.800
It's no big deal, really.

00:09:29.800 --> 00:09:34.070
Sure, if it wasn't for him,
I would have never been born.

00:09:34.070 --> 00:09:38.610
But that's all it is. We don't live together.

00:09:38.610 --> 00:09:41.580
I would go on living, even if he wasn't around.

00:09:41.580 --> 00:09:44.450
Just today, I wished he wasn't here.

00:09:44.450 --> 00:09:47.250
You don't like your father?

00:09:47.250 --> 00:09:49.550
If that's what you think, then, yeah.

00:09:49.550 --> 00:09:54.820
But that's not what he thinks.
He's giving you shelter, Sigelinde.

00:09:54.820 --> 00:09:59.290
That's because I'm the heiress
to the Baumgard family.

00:09:59.290 --> 00:10:01.500
Are you sure?

00:10:01.500 --> 00:10:04.400
It's not as though he likes me.

00:10:04.400 --> 00:10:08.100
The family name is just important to him.

00:10:08.100 --> 00:10:10.300
I don't get it.

00:10:10.300 --> 00:10:12.740
Then don't ask me about it.

00:10:16.510 --> 00:10:19.480
This is not where I belong.

00:10:34.200 --> 00:10:35.830
Where are you going?

00:10:35.830 --> 00:10:39.630
I can't sleep. I'm going out
to get some night air.

00:10:57.190 --> 00:10:59.020
Toa...

00:10:59.020 --> 00:11:03.480
Ah, that was refreshing.
Gio, you should shower, too.

00:11:06.560 --> 00:11:09.830
Huh? Where did he go?

00:11:27.550 --> 00:11:29.140
What's that?

00:11:50.840 --> 00:11:52.500
Itsuki...

00:12:40.720 --> 00:12:44.160
Oh, so you're at the Baumgard Mansion?

00:12:44.160 --> 00:12:47.760
Yeah, we've eaten, and we're
through the first part of this.

00:12:47.760 --> 00:12:50.500
How nice, having dinner at a mansion.

00:12:50.500 --> 00:12:55.340
I wouldn't say that.
By the way, any ISDA activity?

00:12:55.340 --> 00:12:59.070
Habaragi ltsuki and Otohime
were taken into custody.

00:12:59.070 --> 00:13:02.480
They should be locked up on
Tartarus within the evening.

00:13:02.480 --> 00:13:06.610
So the only Dragons left now are Toa and Gio.

00:13:06.610 --> 00:13:09.680
Also, the science team
has been acting strangely.

00:13:09.680 --> 00:13:11.150
How so?

00:13:11.150 --> 00:13:14.490
They're moving people and equipment to Tartarus.

00:13:14.490 --> 00:13:15.920
Which means...

00:13:15.920 --> 00:13:18.980
They're planning to use
the Dragons to do something.

00:13:20.930 --> 00:13:24.130
- I'll be in touch.
- Just a minute.

00:13:24.130 --> 00:13:25.830
What is it?

00:13:28.040 --> 00:13:30.770
You want a good-night kiss?

00:13:30.770 --> 00:13:34.040
Don't be silly. How is Toa doing?

00:13:34.040 --> 00:13:37.450
- How do you mean?
- Ls there anything different about her?

00:13:37.450 --> 00:13:40.010
No, not really.

00:13:40.010 --> 00:13:42.650
Oh, good.

00:13:42.650 --> 00:13:44.210
Hey!

00:13:49.020 --> 00:13:50.720
Good night.

00:13:55.300 --> 00:13:59.000
P-Professor! It's your back again!

00:13:59.000 --> 00:14:02.170
I'm all right. It'll pass soon.

00:14:02.170 --> 00:14:05.200
- But...
- I'm all right.

00:14:10.040 --> 00:14:14.020
Are you sure about not telling Jin?

00:14:14.020 --> 00:14:17.390
- Yes.
- Someday, he will find out.

00:14:17.390 --> 00:14:21.090
I know. But not now.

00:14:21.090 --> 00:14:23.090
You don't have much time.

00:14:23.090 --> 00:14:24.680
Mm-hmm.

00:14:25.990 --> 00:14:28.390
Gio? What's the matter?

00:14:30.160 --> 00:14:32.330
Hey, Gio?

00:14:45.780 --> 00:14:48.910
Gio? What's the matter?

00:14:51.390 --> 00:14:53.050
It's nothing.

00:14:55.190 --> 00:14:59.130
No matter what happens, I will protect Toa.

00:14:59.130 --> 00:15:01.790
Where did Gio go off to?

00:15:06.270 --> 00:15:08.240
Is something the matter?

00:15:08.240 --> 00:15:12.210
Oh, no, my companion left our room,
and hasn't come back.

00:15:12.210 --> 00:15:14.540
I'm wondering if he's gotten lost.

00:15:14.540 --> 00:15:16.740
I'm out looking for him.

00:15:19.380 --> 00:15:21.040
Um...

00:15:22.480 --> 00:15:26.120
My father enjoyed this country,

00:15:26.120 --> 00:15:30.120
and often made time to
come here to this mansion.

00:15:30.120 --> 00:15:31.990
Is that right?

00:15:31.990 --> 00:15:37.430
After Sigelinde was born,
he made sure to bring her along.

00:15:37.430 --> 00:15:39.470
He was a strict father.

00:15:39.470 --> 00:15:43.100
I don't remember ever having him play with me.

00:15:43.100 --> 00:15:46.340
But he pampered that granddaughter of his.

00:15:46.340 --> 00:15:49.740
Um, where is Sigelinde's mother?

00:15:49.740 --> 00:15:53.650
She died soon after Sigelinde was born.

00:15:53.650 --> 00:15:55.280
I'm sorry.

00:15:55.280 --> 00:15:56.980
It's okay.

00:15:58.420 --> 00:16:02.860
I lied about having a meeting here in Japan.

00:16:02.860 --> 00:16:05.130
When I heard that she was being pursued,

00:16:05.130 --> 00:16:08.100
I thought that she might flee to this place.

00:16:08.100 --> 00:16:10.970
So then, why are you here?

00:16:10.970 --> 00:16:16.300
I want to help my daughter.
Isn't that enough of a reason?

00:16:16.300 --> 00:16:19.370
Then, why don't you tell her so?

00:16:19.370 --> 00:16:21.640
Don't talk about honor or inheritances,

00:16:21.640 --> 00:16:24.710
just come out and say you want to help her,

00:16:24.710 --> 00:16:27.450
and that you're worried about her.

00:16:27.450 --> 00:16:32.150
She doesn't like me. The only ones
she's ever opened her heart to

00:16:32.150 --> 00:16:34.890
have been my father and Amadeus.

00:16:34.890 --> 00:16:36.520
Amadeus?

00:16:36.520 --> 00:16:39.150
That's the name of the dog she had.

00:16:41.900 --> 00:16:46.670
Neither my father nor Amadeus are still with us.

00:16:46.670 --> 00:16:52.510
Once we've got everything ready,
we're going to sneak into ISDA.

00:16:52.510 --> 00:16:55.340
It's a plan more dangerous than
anything we've done before.

00:16:55.340 --> 00:16:59.250
There's no guarantee that
we'll be coming back safely.

00:16:59.250 --> 00:17:04.650
So, please, tell Sigelinde
how you feel about her.

00:17:04.650 --> 00:17:09.560
But it doesn't matter what I say to her...

00:17:09.560 --> 00:17:12.190
Forgive me for interrupting
you while you're busy.

00:17:12.190 --> 00:17:14.930
It looks like we won't be able
to take our time any longer.

00:17:14.930 --> 00:17:17.570
It sounds like Howling Star
and the others are in trouble.

00:17:17.570 --> 00:17:20.530
I wish we could have prepared a little bit more.

00:17:20.530 --> 00:17:22.040
Then, when?

00:17:22.040 --> 00:17:24.060
We leave as soon as day breaks.

00:17:29.610 --> 00:17:31.670
Tomorrow?

00:17:39.520 --> 00:17:43.520
Habaragi ltsuki and Otohime
have been locked up on Tartarus.

00:17:43.520 --> 00:17:45.360
I will be returning now.

00:17:45.360 --> 00:17:46.950
Well done.

00:17:50.870 --> 00:17:53.370
Here I was wondering how to dispose of you,

00:17:53.370 --> 00:17:56.300
once Thanatos has been taken care of,

00:17:56.300 --> 00:17:59.270
but what a convenient tool you'll turn out to be

00:17:59.270 --> 00:18:02.210
if you die on your own,
without me having to do anything.

00:18:16.490 --> 00:18:19.390
Commander, the anti-Thanatos
factor that we injected

00:18:19.390 --> 00:18:22.160
into Howling Star and Amadeus
has been eradicated.

00:18:22.160 --> 00:18:23.630
What happened?

00:18:23.630 --> 00:18:26.270
All we can figure is that the
antibodies within the two of them

00:18:26.270 --> 00:18:28.100
took hold of the anti-Thanatos factor,

00:18:28.100 --> 00:18:31.670
and their macrophages
displayed remarkable power.

00:18:31.670 --> 00:18:35.180
So what you're saying is,
there is an immunoreaction at work?

00:18:35.180 --> 00:18:40.920
Yes. But we didn't see any immune
function operating in the Raum

00:18:40.920 --> 00:18:43.980
and Album samples, and their
dysplasia is still proceeding.

00:18:43.980 --> 00:18:49.460
So then, the anti-Thanatos factor
is only effective in Original Dragons?

00:18:49.460 --> 00:18:53.490
Probably. I think that's safe to say.

00:18:53.490 --> 00:18:56.600
Now that we've lost the Raum, unless we capture

00:18:56.600 --> 00:19:01.590
the Album or the Atrum and test it
on them, we cannot say for sure.

00:19:05.670 --> 00:19:07.270
Commander?

00:19:07.270 --> 00:19:09.040
I'll give you my order later.

00:19:09.040 --> 00:19:10.670
Acknowledged.

00:19:13.150 --> 00:19:18.110
It only works on Original Dragons, does it?

00:19:30.970 --> 00:19:33.400
This really is perfect.

00:19:43.680 --> 00:19:46.380
I'm asking you to return home.

00:19:46.380 --> 00:19:49.420
Are you telling me to come and
take over the Baumgard family?

00:19:49.420 --> 00:19:50.880
If so, then I...

00:19:50.880 --> 00:19:53.050
No!

00:19:53.050 --> 00:19:59.820
I'm asking you if you would come home
to your father, as his daughter.

00:20:01.730 --> 00:20:03.660
Father...

00:20:17.440 --> 00:20:24.420
A girl who hated her strict father,
but took to her doting grandfather...

00:20:24.420 --> 00:20:29.790
Families are all the same,
whether rich or poor, huh?

00:20:29.790 --> 00:20:33.890
I'm not convinced that
Sigelinde really hates her father.

00:20:33.890 --> 00:20:37.800
There's no way she could.
The two of them are just, you know,

00:20:37.800 --> 00:20:42.870
unsure about how to go about
patching things up between them.

00:20:42.870 --> 00:20:44.600
Patching things up...

00:20:48.110 --> 00:20:49.580
Let's go.

00:20:49.580 --> 00:20:51.610
You mean we're not waiting for Sigelinde?

00:20:51.610 --> 00:20:54.450
- Yep.
- But...

00:20:54.450 --> 00:20:57.950
Sigelinde should stay behind
here, and live a happy life.

00:20:57.950 --> 00:21:00.420
Where do you get off deciding that for me,

00:21:00.420 --> 00:21:02.120
little man?!

00:21:02.120 --> 00:21:04.760
Sigelinde...

00:21:04.760 --> 00:21:06.660
Do you mean to tell me that the
bond between father and child

00:21:06.660 --> 00:21:08.430
is the most precious thing in the world?

00:21:08.430 --> 00:21:13.170
You ought to know that there are
things that are even more important!

00:21:13.170 --> 00:21:17.810
No, you can't tell me you don't
know that! No way, no how!

00:21:17.810 --> 00:21:20.470
Right now, I belong with the Dragonauts!

00:21:20.470 --> 00:21:24.140
And we need Amadeus!

00:21:24.140 --> 00:21:25.840
Sigelinde...

00:22:19.330 --> 00:22:21.570
You don't even think hard about the meaning

00:22:21.570 --> 00:22:23.870
of the words you spit out

00:22:23.870 --> 00:22:28.210
you just run away from the present

00:22:28.210 --> 00:22:30.480
Still doing the same things over and over,

00:22:30.480 --> 00:22:32.580
like nothing has happened

00:22:32.580 --> 00:22:36.250
It makes no sense to run away again

00:22:36.250 --> 00:22:45.160
In the end, you're immature,
still a child, complacent

00:22:45.160 --> 00:22:54.570
Leave behind your old self already

00:22:54.570 --> 00:22:59.070
The righteous fight starts within you

00:22:59.070 --> 00:23:03.510
What would you do?
You're out of time, aren't you?

00:23:03.510 --> 00:23:08.580
Try to remember how you're supposed to be

00:23:08.580 --> 00:23:15.690
before it all falls apart

00:23:15.690 --> 00:23:21.790
Fight or flight

00:23:24.460 --> 00:23:29.270
Fight or flight

00:23:42.380 --> 00:23:43.620
Welcome!

00:23:43.620 --> 00:23:46.490
One Shin-Ogasawara sandwich, to go.

00:23:46.490 --> 00:23:49.490
I'll have 12 of the Dragon Burgers.

00:23:49.490 --> 00:23:52.460
- Huh? You're going to eat that many?!
- Yes, I am.

00:23:52.460 --> 00:23:57.160
I'm terribly sorry, we discontinued
the Dragon Burger last week.

00:23:57.160 --> 00:24:01.070
Hmm... ah, well then, one preview.

00:24:01.070 --> 00:24:06.110
Right! Next time, there's gonna
be a desperate rescue mission!

00:24:06.110 --> 00:24:08.940
Oh, I forgot my wallet!
